# Env and secrets.
#
# The `**/` forms are required, for the same reason node_modules is doubled up above:
# Docker matches these patterns against the whole relative path, so a bare `.env`
# covers only the context root. Without them `deploy/aws/.env` stays in the build
# context — measured, not assumed: appending one line to it changed both image asset
# hashes, so a configuration-only change rebuilt and re-pushed both images. Not a
# secret leak (every COPY in the Dockerfiles is explicit and narrow; none reaches
# `deploy/`), but it defeats the point of a config-driven target.
#
# Deliberately NO `!**/.env.example` counterpart. A `**` *negation* forces CDK's asset
# fingerprint to descend into every excluded directory to check for re-includes, which
# defeats directory pruning: measured at 6.7 s -> 59.4 s of synth, a 9x regression, on
# a tree carrying node_modules and a 465 MB cdk.out. The `**` *excludes* above are
# free (7.2 s) — it is only the negation that costs. Nothing needs it either: no
# Dockerfile in this repo COPYs any `.env*`, so the example files are wanted in git,
# not in an image. `!.env.example` below is kept for the context root only, where the
# absence of `**` leaves pruning intact.
#
# Pinned by deploy/aws/lib/config/env-file-churn.test.ts.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example

# Misc
*.log
.DS_Store
*.plan.md

# Git worktrees. The Agentic SDLC creates one per parallel story (AGENTS.md
# § Worktrees), each a full checkout of the repo — 3 GB on a machine running two —
# and none of it belongs in a build context. Docker would copy it; CDK's
# DockerImageAsset walks it to compute the asset fingerprint, which is slower still
# because that happens on every synth.
.worktrees
**/.worktrees

# CDK synth output, including staged assets from a previous run.
cdk.out
**/cdk.out

# The committed CDK template, which `pnpm synth` rewrites. It lives inside the build
# context, so leaving it here makes the image asset hash a function of the previous
# synth's output: each run rewrites the snapshot, which changes the context, which
# changes the asset hash, which changes the migrate trigger's IMAGE_IDENTIFIER and the
# Lambda Version logical ID derived from it. `synth:check` then reports drift forever.
cdk.snapshot
**/cdk.snapshot
